# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  packages.live-only — what is on the ISO ON PURPOSE and not on a disk
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  This file is the declared difference between packages.x86_64 (the ISO) and
#  packages.install (an installed machine). tools/check.sh requires every ISO
#  package to be in one of the two: either the installed machine gets it, or
#  the reason it does not is written down here.
#
#  Without that, the two lists drift apart in silence — which is exactly what
#  happened: the ISO became STYLUS and the installer went on installing the
#  distribution it was inherited from, with an office suite and no music.
#
#  Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── the installer itself ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
arch-install-scripts
archinstall

# ── the initramfs and the boot menu OF THE MEDIUM ──────────────────────────
# An installed system boots through GRUB and an ordinary initramfs.
mkinitcpio-archiso
mkinitcpio-nfs-utils
syslinux
edk2-shell
refind
memtest86+
memtest86+-efi

# ── reading the medium's own compressed filesystem ─────────────────────────
squashfs-tools

# ── virtual machine guest tools ────────────────────────────────────────────
# They exist so the ISO can be TRIED in a VM before it is given a disk. On a
# real machine they are four services looking for a hypervisor that is not
# there.
qemu-guest-agent
open-vm-tools
virtualbox-guest-utils-nox
hyperv

# ── networking before NetworkManager ───────────────────────────────────────
# The medium comes up on dhcpcd/iwd so there is a network at the console
# straight away. An installed system uses NetworkManager, and all three
# fighting over one interface is a classic.
dhcpcd
iwd

# ── prebuilt Broadcom wifi ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# broadcom-wl matches the `linux` kernel alone, and an install also lays down
# linux-lts. The installer detects the card and uses broadcom-wl-dkms, which
# is rebuilt for every kernel — the emergency one included.
broadcom-wl
b43-fwcutter

# ── rescue ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rescue-medium tools: what they are for is a disk that is NOT mounted.
ddrescue
testdisk

# ── one graphics driver per vendor ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The ISO carries all of them because it has to come up on a stranger's
# computer. By install time the card is known and the installer picks (see
# MESA_SET and GPU_PKGS in stylus-install); keeping all three here would cost
# disk and make pacman rebuild things nobody uses.
vulkan-radeon
lib32-vulkan-radeon
vulkan-intel
lib32-vulkan-intel
vulkan-nouveau
lib32-vulkan-nouveau
intel-media-driver
vpl-gpu-rt
